  "body": "**Wanted:** a short guide for router users: a sheet cut-out with tabs from a drawing, and a V-carved name once #1443 lands. It ships with a demo project and a recorded air-cut check. It's the first page a DeskProto or VCarve user should find. It depends on the DXF-to-cuts issues (#1864 / #1867 / #1869) and the guided sheet job issue.\n\n**Done means:** the guide is published on the docs site with its demo project, and every step in it works on the current release.\n\nPart of #3066 (findings: https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/3066#issuecomment-7050655107). The clean-room boundary of #3066 applies: no vendor wording, labels, parameter names or dialog flows.",
